WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.812 --> 00:00:10.878 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to the North America capitals, episode five of five. First, I clear
the chosen names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:11.529 --> 00:00:18.774 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
And four close the series: the Windward islands and Barbados, and the great
island of Trinidad at their foot.

3
00:00:19.429 --> 00:00:21.554 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Saint George's into view.

4
00:00:25.042 --> 00:00:33.958 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Saint George's stands on the Carenage, a horseshoe harbour, on the west coast
of Grenada, with the houses climbing the hills around it.

5
00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:41.987 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The French founded it in 1650, and American troops landed here in 1983.

6
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:49.895 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Saint George's as the horseshoe harbour, founded by the French and
landed on by Americans in 1983.

7
00:00:50.576 --> 00:00:52.573 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Kingstown into view.

8
00:00:56.158 --> 00:01:03.194 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Kingstown stands on the windward shore of Saint Vincent, below the green
slopes of the central mountains.

9
00:01:03.847 --> 00:01:16.897 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its botanic garden, of 1765, is the oldest in the Americas, and Captain Bligh
brought breadfruit trees to it. It is called the city of arches, for its stone
arcades.

10
00:01:17.552 --> 00:01:24.541 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Kingstown as the city of arches, with the oldest botanic garden in
the Americas.

11
00:01:25.225 --> 00:01:27.524 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Bridgetown into view.

12
00:01:30.704 --> 00:01:37.914 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Bridgetown stands on Carlisle Bay in the west of Barbados, an island of coral
limestone in the Atlantic.

13
00:01:38.578 --> 00:01:56.326 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its old town and British garrison are a UNESCO site, and its Parliament,
meeting since 1639, is one of the oldest in the Commonwealth. George
Washington stayed here in 1751, on the only journey he ever made abroad.

14
00:01:56.975 --> 00:02:05.636 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Bridgetown as the Parliament that has met since 1639, and the only
country George Washington ever visited abroad.

15
00:02:06.322 --> 00:02:09.341 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Port-of-Spain into view.

16
00:02:11.757 --> 00:02:20.801 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Port-of-Spain stands on the Gulf of Paria, on the north-west coast of
Trinidad, facing Venezuela across the water.

17
00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:31.224 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its carnival is the largest in the Caribbean, and its Queen's Park Savannah is
often called one of the largest roundabouts in the world.

18
00:02:31.889 --> 00:02:38.878 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Port-of-Spain as the carnival capital, with a savannah that counts as
a roundabout.

19
00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:54.317 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Saint George's and Kingstown stand on the Grenadines and Saint Vincent,
Bridgetown on the Atlantic side of Barbados, and Port-of-Spain on the Gulf of
Paria.

20
00:02:54.972 --> 00:03:06.489 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the horseshoe harbour, the city of arches with the oldest botanic
garden in the Americas, the Parliament that has met since 1639, and the
carnival capital with a savannah roundabout.
